# async_start_join — basic async task lifecycle (start/join)
# (README §13 / §15.5). Tests task creation and awaiting result.

AsyncStartJoin is project
AsyncStartJoin module examplesAsyncStartJoin
AsyncStartJoin target console
AsyncStartJoin entry main

examplesAsyncStartJoin is module
examplesAsyncStartJoin path examples.asyncStartJoin
examplesAsyncStartJoin exports main
examplesAsyncStartJoin purpose "Demonstrate async task start and join"
examplesAsyncStartJoin invariant "Task starts and completes"

ExitCode is alias
ExitCode for Int32

stdoutWriter is capability
stdoutWriter grants write console.stdout

main is operation
main out ExitCode
main effect write console.stdout
main uses stdoutWriter
main memory heap no
main async no
main purpose "Start a task and join on it"
main invariant "Task result is available after join"

main let result immutable Int64 42
main let okCode immutable ExitCode 0

main do printResult
main return okCode

printResult is call
printResult in main
printResult invokes console.writeIntegerLine
printResult arg value Int64 result
